sparky-stereo-browser (@DEBVERSION@) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The flat WebXR display (an inline-stereo session, WebXR 3.4, drawn through
    the page's canvas) gives the eyes the person's depth limit as the screen
    has it, whatever the width of the window: the limits are set once, for the
    screen, in pixels of a view as wide as the output, and the separation is
    that share of the output's width over the width the canvas is shown at,
    the same conversion as the 3D Canvas camera. Before, the separation was
    the limit over 1920 times the canvas's own width, so a window half as wide
    showed half the separation. An immersive session fills the output and is
    unchanged. The browser has no new setting.

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  @DATE@
